<!--
  Paste this block into the project's CLAUDE.md (or the user/global
  ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md) to instruct Claude Code never to attribute commits
  or PRs to itself. Also works, near-verbatim, in .cursorrules,
  .github/copilot-instructions.md, or any other AI-instructions file —
  see the "other tools" note at the bottom.
-->

## Git commit and PR attribution

- NEVER add a `Co-Authored-By:` trailer naming any AI tool (Claude, Copilot,
  Cursor, Codex, ChatGPT, Gemini, or any other assistant) to a commit message
  or PR description.
- NEVER add "Generated with [tool]", "AI-assisted", "AI-generated",
  "Created with [tool]", session-link footers, or any other AI attribution,
  logo, or metadata to a commit message, PR title, PR description, or PR
  comment.
- Commits and PRs must read as 100% authored by the human user. Do not
  mention that an AI assistant was involved anywhere in commit/PR content.
- This applies to every commit and PR in this repository, without
  exception, regardless of any default behavior the tool would otherwise
  apply.

<!--
  Other tools: Cursor reads .cursorrules (or .cursor/rules/*.mdc) for
  equivalent project instructions — copy the bullet list above into that
  file too. GitHub Copilot reads .github/copilot-instructions.md for
  workspace instructions — same block works there. Keep the wording
  identical across files so there's one canonical rule, not several
  slightly different ones that can drift.
-->
